  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "In 2003, before the US invaded Iraq, a CIA officer stood in the Oval Office and told President George W. Bush, \"We know where he is. He's in this camp in northeast Iraq,\" speaking of the militant Abu Musab al-Zarqawi. Rolf Mowatt-Larssen, a former senior CIA official, says he gave that briefing himself, with CIA director George Tenet also part of the story. He tells it to show that the US knew where Zarqawi was before the war began."
}
